# Website external links (off-site)

Any link that takes the user **off shroffin.com** (RBI, Income Tax, NHB, WhatsApp web destinations in guide body, government portals, insurer sites, etc.) must use the **exact** `guide-section-link` pattern from `pages/tax-benefits.html` (Section 22↗). Do not invent a new look each time.

## Always

1. Use class `guide-section-link` on the `<a>`.
2. Open in a new tab: `target="_blank"` + `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
3. Visible off-site cue: `<span class="guide-section-link-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>`.
4. Screen-reader purpose: `<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens official [Site] page)</span>` — name the destination (RBI, Income Tax, NHB, etc.).
5. Visible label = the real thing (Section 22, RBI Master Directions, cms.rbi.org.in) — not “click here” or “learn more”.
6. If the page is missing styles, copy the CSS block for `.guide-section-link` / `.guide-section-link-arrow` (and `.visually-hidden` if absent) from `pages/tax-benefits.html`.

## Markup (copy this shape)

```html
<a
  class="guide-section-link"
  href="https://example.gov.in/..."
  target="_blank"
  rel="noopener noreferrer"
>Label<span class="guide-section-link-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="visually-hidden"> (opens official Example page)</span></a>
```

Title-adjacent small note (optional wrapper): wrap in `<span class="guide-limit-note">…</span>` like Section 22 on tax benefits.

Inline in body: same `<a class="guide-section-link">` inside `.guide-share-then` (CSS already targets that).

## Never

- Plain blue `<a href="https://…">` without `guide-section-link`, ↗, and visually-hidden text.
- ↗ only as loose text with no classes.
- Off-site links without `target="_blank"` / `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Using this pattern for **same-site** links (other Shroffin pages, in-page `#anchors`).

## Exceptions

- **Global nav WhatsApp** may keep `Chat on WhatsApp ↗` in the submenu label (existing `globalnav-submenu-link` pattern). Do not convert nav to `guide-section-link`.
- Mailto / tel links stay as normal contacts — no ↗ unless they open an external web app in a new tab by design.

## Quick self-check

Off-site? → `guide-section-link` + ↗ + visually-hidden + blank tab. Same site? → normal internal link, no ↗.
